Package: remlax
Type: Package
Title: Generic, Differentiable REML Solver for Linear Mixed Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Nicolas", family = "Salas",
                  email = "nicolas.salas@supagro.fr",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R interface to the 'remlax' solver, which maximises the restricted
    likelihood of linear mixed models with an asreml-like formula grammar. The
    likelihood is formed on the dense marginal covariance and differentiated
    automatically by a 'JAX' solver that runs unchanged on CPU or GPU. The R side
    builds and checks the design, writes it to a directory as raw binary plus a
    JSON manifest, calls the solver as a subprocess, and reads the result back.
    Covariance structures follow the ASReml-R catalogue (idv, idh, corgh, fa,
    rr, chol, ante, corh; ar1, ar2, ar3, ma, arma, corb, corg, exp, gau, sph,
    cir, Matern, separable products). A second, sparse engine built on 'RTMB'
    covers the subset of structures whose precision is sparse and known in
    closed form. The Python solver ships with the package; a Python (>= 3.10)
    interpreter with 'jax', 'numpy' and 'scipy' must be available, and
    rx_install_python() creates one on request. The validation against
    'asreml', 'lme4', 'sommer' and 'nlme' is shipped as a vignette, and
    rx_validate() reruns the comparisons against the CRAN packages.
License: GPL (>= 3)
